// Enchant = the Aura's quality restriction [CR#702.5a]: "Enchant [quality]"
// parameterizes the legal-host predicate. The quality is a card-type
// characteristic (`Type(Creature)`, the form keyword qualities share with
// Protection and Affinity), and an object description naming a card type means
// a permanent of that type on the battlefield [CR#109.2]. So every use below
// reads it as `And([Permanent, Param(0)])`: the Aura spell targets, may be
// attached to, and as it enters chooses only such a permanent, never a card in
// a hand or graveyard. The keyword confers THREE abilities (spec conferral
// map):
//   1. a targeting `Spell` carrying ONLY the target spec ([CR#303.4a]) — its
//      no-op `Sequentially([])` effect keeps cast targeting on the live
//      `spell_targets` path; it does not attach.
//   2. a *removable* `May(Attach(what: Ref(This), to: Param(0)))` — the
//      legal-host grant ([CR#702.5a]) under default-deny attachment (being
//      attachable to a matching quality is a granted capability); also a
//      sibling `Cant(Target)` so the spell can't target an illegal quality.
//   3. the `AsEnters(Attach(...))` self-replacement ([CR#303.4,303.4f]) — the
//      SOLE attach-on-entry. The verb `Attach` takes a single `Reference` host
//      now, so choosing the host is a separate pre-attach step: as it enters,
//      the controller chooses a legal host matching the enchant quality, bound
//      as the choice frame, then the Aura attaches to it — `With(binder:
//      ChooseOne(filter: Param(0)), body: Attach(This, It))`. Written as the inlined
//      `Also(would: ThisEnters, also: …)` form (what `AsEnters` expands to)
//      because Enchant's `Param(0)` can't thread through a nested macro call's
//      arguments — the engine recognizes this `With(ChooseOne(quality),
//      Attach(This, It))` shape directly (replace.rs `enters_attached_quality`).
// The must-be-attached graveyard SBA ([CR#704.5m]) is the AURA SUBTYPE's Innate
// rule, NOT this keyword (the subtype/ability decoupling — spec §"finding").
(
    name: "Enchant",
    template: "enchant ${0}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Enchant",
        abilities: [
            Spell(
                effect: Targeted(
                    targets: [Target(Exactly(1), And([Permanent, Param(0)]))],
                    effect: Sequentially([]),
                ),
            ),
            Static(Cant(Target(by: (stack_object: Ref(This)), on: Not(And([Permanent, Param(0)]))))),
            Static(May(Attach(what: Ref(This), to: And([Permanent, Param(0)])))),
            Static(Replacement(Also(
                would: ThisEnters,
                also: With(
                    binder: ChooseOne(filter: And([Permanent, Param(0)])),
                    body: Attach(what: This, to: It),
                ),
            ))),
        ],
    ),
)
